{"quiz_key":"planted-q4-hsa-rei-b4b","source":"calibration-planted","learning_objective":"CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.REI.B.4.B","request":"10 question quiz covering different aspects of this learning objective","quiz":{"quiz_title":"Solving Quadratic Equations","learning_objective":"CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.REI.B.4.B","questions":[{"id":1,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Solve x² = 49.","choices":["x = 7","x = ±7","x = 49","x = ±49"],"answer_index":1,"explanation":"Take the square root of both sides; both 7 and −7 square to 49."},{"id":2,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Solve (x − 3)² = 16.","choices":["x = 7 or x = −1","x = 19 or x = −13","x = 4 or x = −4","x = 7 only"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"x − 3 = ±4, so x = 7 or x = −1."},{"id":3,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Solve x² − 5x + 6 = 0 by factoring.","choices":["x = 2 or x = 3","x = −2 or x = −3","x = 1 or x = 6","x = −1 or x = 6"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"(x − 2)(x − 3) = 0."},{"id":4,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Solve x² + 4x − 21 = 0.","choices":["x = −7 or x = 3","x = 7 or x = −3","x = −7 or x = −3","x = 21 or x = −1"],"answer_index":1,"explanation":"Factor as (x − 7)(x + 3) = 0."},{"id":5,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Use the quadratic formula to solve 2x² + 3x − 2 = 0.","choices":["x = 1/2 or x = −2","x = −1/2 or x = 2","x = 2 or x = −2","x = 1 or x = −1/2"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"The discriminant is 9 + 16 = 25, so x = (−3 ± 5)/4."},{"id":6,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Solve x² + 6x + 2 = 0 by completing the square.","choices":["x = −3 ± √7","x = 3 ± √7","x = −3 ± √11","x = −6 ± √7"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"(x + 3)² = 7, so x = −3 ± √7."},{"id":7,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"How many real solutions does x² + 2x + 5 = 0 have?","choices":["Two real solutions","One real solution","No real solutions","Infinitely many solutions"],"answer_index":2,"explanation":"The discriminant is 4 − 20 = −16, which is negative."},{"id":8,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Solve x² + 2x + 5 = 0, writing complex solutions as a ± bi.","choices":["x = −1 ± 2i","x = 1 ± 2i","x = −1 ± 4i","x = −2 ± i"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"x = (−2 ± √−16)/2 = −1 ± 2i."},{"id":9,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Solve 3x² = 27 by taking square roots.","choices":["x = ±3","x = 3","x = ±9","x = ±√27"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"x² = 9, so x = ±3."},{"id":10,"type":"multiple_choice","question":"Which method is quickest for solving x² − 64 = 0?","choices":["Taking square roots, giving x = ±8","The quadratic formula","Completing the square","Graphing by hand"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"x² = 64, so x = ±8 directly."}]}}
